p10. The test-gate observation on bitpack-write-contend-shared, raw.

Not a probe I wrote: this is the captured output of the gate runs themselves,
kept because 100 section 0 cites it and a citation to a transcript nobody kept
is not a citation.

THREE RUNS OF ONE CRATE, same host, same pin:

  1. debug, cargo test, default parallel runner
     killed by me at 58 minutes elapsed, having produced no test result line.
  2. release, cargo test, default parallel runner
     killed by me at 37 minutes elapsed. Its tail is reproduced below.
  3. debug, test binary invoked directly with --test-threads=1
     15 passed in 45.22 seconds.

I KILLED 1 AND 2, so what is established is that they had not finished at those
elapsed times, NOT that they never would. Run 3 is a completed measurement.

--- tail of run 2, release, default parallel runner ---
test stress::stress_size_is_actually_misaligned ... ok
test kernels::tests::windowed_agrees_split_across_period_aligned_calls ... ok
test kernels::tests::sequential_split_guarded_agrees_misaligned ... ok
test kernels::tests::sequential_split_plain_agrees_aligned ... ok
test kernels::tests::sequential_split_plain_agrees_even_misaligned ... ok
test stress::guarded_kernel_never_corrupts_under_real_concurrency has been running for over 60 seconds
test stress::naive_kernel_corruption_rate_under_real_concurrency has been running for over 60 seconds
test stress::naive_kernel_never_corrupts_when_the_split_is_aligned has been running for over 60 seconds

--- run 3, complete ---
running 15 tests
... (all 15 listed, all ok)
test result: ok. 15 passed; 0 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 0 filtered out; finished in 45.22s

READING

The three stress tests run CONCURRENTLY under the default runner and each is
reported by the runner as exceeding 60 seconds. The crate declares a single
per-process four-thread pool (src/stress.rs:66-72) that every stress test
shares. Three tests contending for one four-thread pool is the mechanism, and
the release profile ruling out compilation as the explanation is what makes it
the mechanism rather than a guess.
